    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0268" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/3–2151</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marshall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-03-21">March 21, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Acheson</hi>: I am returning in a very informal
                    manner, in order to save time, the suggestions of the Joint Chiefs of Staff
                    regarding <pb facs="0269" n="253" xml:id="pg253"/> a proposed presidential
                    statement on Korea and my own suggestions.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d176-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Those of the Joint Chiefs of Staff are indicated on Page 2 in blue ink.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d176-f2"/> My suggestions are indicated in red ink—in the
                    second line by striking out the word “the” and by the letter “X” opposite
                    certain paragraphs which I think might well be omitted in order to make the
                    statement shorter and more incisive. However, that is a mere suggestion of
                        mine.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d176-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d176-a1.xml" xpointer="d176-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d176-f1" n="1" xml:id="d176-f1-content">
                <p>The text of the draft statement is printed as an annex to this memorandum, below,
                    with the suggestions of Secretary Marshall and the Joint Chiefs of Staff
                    indicated in subsequent footnotes.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d176-f2" n="2" xml:id="d176-f2-content">
                <p>See footnotes 5 and 6, below.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d176-f3" n="3" xml:id="d176-f3-content">
                <p>None of Secretary Marshall’s suggestions were incorporated in the proposed
                    statement. The paragraphs marked by him with an “x” for possible omission were
                    the third, fifth, and tenth.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
